 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "processCommand takes single-space-separated tokens and returns a string. Integer fields must match -?(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,8}) (otherwise ERROR). REGISTER <name> <lat> <lon> <capacity> stores a healthy datacenter with load 0 and returns OK when the name is new, -90<=lat<=90, -180<=lon<=180 and capacity>=1, else ERROR. ROUTE <lat> <lon> (same ranges) picks, among healthy datacenters with load < capacity, the one with the smallest squared Euclidean distance, then smaller load, then smaller name (code point order); it increments that load and returns its name, or ERROR if none qualifies (sentinel inferred). Any other keyword or token count returns ERROR without changing state. Level 2 adds DOWN <name> and UP <name>: set the health of a registered datacenter and return OK (even if unchanged), ERROR for an unknown name. Unhealthy datacenters are skipped by ROUTE.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk04-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
